      "summary": ": Today's Ski Summary 12 August 2026 — 12:48 PM NZ time: Treble Cone is OPEN, with Home Basin the place to be. The resort has completed plenty of overnight grooming, so freshly prepared terrain is ready for early laps. Northerly winds are expected to strengthen through the day, particularly across higher and more exposed areas, with precipitation also expected. These conditions may affect lift operations as the day progresses, so skiers should keep checking the latest lift and weather updates. Home Basin Express and the Beginner Platter are open. Saddle Quad is closed, while Saddle Basin and Matukituki Basin are closed for the day. Summit Slopes and Motatapu Chutes are on hold. Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are open. The National Junior Slalom Competition has been postponed today due to the forecast conditions.",
